1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,520
I asked a dead
sign where it was.

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:03,570
It answered.

3
00:00:03,770 --> 00:00:04,030
Nine.

4
00:00:04,030 --> 00:00:04,550
Nine what?

5
00:00:04,550 --> 00:00:04,860
Lives?

6
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:06,040
I'm down to four.

7
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:06,750
Number nine.

8
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:08,590
But this street stops at seven.

9
00:00:08,590 --> 00:00:09,490
That's us.

10
00:00:09,490 --> 00:00:11,190
Great. It's lying. Bedtime.

11
00:00:11,790 --> 00:00:13,910
Working late, Miss Reyes?

12
00:00:13,910 --> 00:00:14,660
Mister Vale.

13
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:16,960
The rent isn't due until Friday.

14
00:00:17,010 --> 00:00:18,760
Oh, I'm not here for rent.

15
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:19,910
I saw your light.

16
00:00:19,910 --> 00:00:22,160
Your mother worked late, too.

17
00:00:22,360 --> 00:00:24,170
What do you know
about my mother?

18
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:27,330
Only that she would not
stop asking questions.

19
00:00:27,330 --> 00:00:28,380
Sleep well.

20
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:29,560
I hate him.

21
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:31,270
He smells like burnt toast.

22
00:00:31,470 --> 00:00:33,740
He walked off, to
where the street ends.

23
00:00:33,740 --> 00:00:35,350
And he never came back.

24
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:36,960
So we went to look.

25
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:39,670
That wall did not
have a door yesterday.

26
00:00:39,970 --> 00:00:41,220
It was nailed shut.

27
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:42,580
From the inside.

28
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:44,700
Then please, please
do not knock.

29
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:46,000
I knocked.

30
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:50,110
I would like to go home now.
